Testing list slice (jar) method:
  Original list: [Axmed, Barwaaqo, Cali, Deeqa, Ergada]
Basic slicing:
  magacyo.jar(1, 3): [Barwaaqo, Cali]
  Original list after slicing: [Axmed, Barwaaqo, Cali, Deeqa, Ergada]
Slicing to the end:
  magacyo.jar(2, magacyo.dherer()): [Cali, Deeqa, Ergada]
Slicing from the beginning:
  magacyo.jar(0, 2): [Axmed, Barwaaqo]
Using negative indices:
  magacyo.jar(-2, magacyo.dherer()): [Deeqa, Ergada]
Empty slice (start equals end):
  magacyo.jar(2, 2): []
Out of range indices:
  magacyo.jar(10, 20): []
  magacyo.jar(-10, 2): [Axmed, Barwaaqo]
Edge cases:
  magacyo.jar(3, 1): []
  magacyo.jar(0, magacyo.dherer()): [Axmed, Barwaaqo, Cali, Deeqa, Ergada]
  Is it a new list (not the same reference)? been
Practical example: pagination
  Items per page: 3
  Page 3: [7, 8, 9]
Working with different data types:
  Mixed list: [10, Somali, run, [1, 2], {name: Soplang}]
  mixed.jar(1, 4): [Somali, run, [1, 2]]
List slice tests completed!
